# The vendored Supabase SDK is verified byte-for-byte against the sha384 the CDN
# published for it - the hash is recorded in the comment above its <script> tag
# in index.html, so that the vendoring can be checked rather than trusted.
#
# git's line-ending translation would rewrite those bytes on checkout (this repo
# is developed on Windows, where core.autocrlf is normally on), the hash would
# stop matching, and the one honest check anybody has on a 214KB minified blob
# would quietly become a lie. So: hands off.
vendor/** -text
